course: dictionary
lesson: 9376
title: Sportive: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sportive is an old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in old books and poems. Like many words, it has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one fits.
explain: In «mon amie Sacha est sportive», the words mon amie tell you Sacha is a girl, and the sentence is in French. English speakers would say «sporty» here. Learners from other languages often use sportive this way, so always check the sentence around it.
explain: The old meaning is playful and full of fun, as in a sportive puppy. In cycling, a sportive is a long, organised bike ride that is not a race, so riders are not trying to beat each other.
fact: Sportive is an adjective that means playful and full of fun, as in a sportive puppy.
fact: Sportive can also mean to do with sport, or sporty in how it looks, such as a sportive car.
fact: A sportive (noun) is a long, organised bike ride that is not a race. It is popular in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Old-fashioned words often appear in old books and poems, not in everyday talk.
fact: In French, «mon ami Camille» means a boy, and «mon amie Sacha est sportive» means a girl who is sporty. Camille and Sacha can be names for boys or girls.
exercise: In the sentence «mon amie Sacha est sportive», is Sacha a boy or a girl? | *A girl | A boy | A dog | A bike
exercise: A sportive is a long, organised bike ride. What kind of event is it? | A dance class | A race with a winner | *A ride that is not a race | A park game
exercise: An old poem says the puppy was sportive and bounced about all day. What does sportive mean here? | Angry and fierce | *Playful and full of fun | Very tired and sleepy | Quiet and still
test: In the phrase a sportive cat chased the ball, what does sportive mean? | *Playful and full of fun | Sad and tired | A long bike ride
test: What does a sportive mean as a noun in cycling? | *A long, organised bike ride that is not a race | A kind of racing bike with a winner | A quiet park walk
exam: Which meaning of sportive fits a sportive car? | *Sporty in how it looks | Playful and full of fun | A long organised bike ride
